      "content": "It's important to monitor your child closely. You can try small sips of an oral rehydration solution (ORS) like Pedialyte or commercially available toddler rehydration drinks. Offer small amounts frequently, but if he isn't drinking, contact a pediatrician for further advice. In the meantime, consider giving him light oral comfort like sugar-free gum or crackers. If he continues to refuse fluids and shows concerning symptoms, seek medical assistance immediately.",
